# Offender models in the orthogonal branch of 13.8.25

The complete offender alternative constructs actual orthogonal section models
in all three source branches. Both strong branches identify the whole actor
with the disjoint-transposition E₁₆ and recognize the literal [W,H] = [W,K]
as the natural module or its augmentation cover. The second branch retains
A₁ noncontainment. The remaining branch derives rank one, recognizes [W,K]
inside W, and marks the actor as the transposition group.

Each alternative uses one marking for the quotient, commutator, actor and
alternating component. The chosen maximal submodule, natural quotient and
earlier critical-pair facts are explicit inputs; the only representation
classification premises are the universal earlier B.4 inputs. Final exclusion
remains with the parent orthogonal argument.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed p.960, PDF p.977.
-/
